<%# The last thing read before the confirm button, because a status change is
    not only a status change: PersonStatusManagement grants and strips positions,
    roles and team memberships behind it, and none of that is visible on the form
    or in the table above.

    Only the moves this page can actually make are described. The statuses that
    strip a record bare -- deceased, dismissed, resigned, uberbonked -- are not
    offered here and are not listed, and neither is anything a locked account
    would do, since the batch refuses those lines outright.

    Two arms because the page has two jobs: the flag changes no status and none
    of this applies to it. %>
<% if batch.action.handler == BulkUpload::StatusHandler %>
  <%= ui_callout_box :warning, icon: "triangle-exclamation", icon_type: :solid do %>
    <strong>A status change does more than change the status.</strong>
    Everyone below gets a row in their status history, and:
    <ul class="list-disc ms-5 mt-2">
      <li><strong>Active</strong> grants every position all Rangers hold, and the roles a new
        account starts with. Coming from Alpha or Bonked, it also grants Dirt - Shiny Penny.</li>
      <li><strong>Alpha</strong> grants the Alpha position.</li>
      <li><strong>Prospective</strong> takes away every position and role, then grants back only
        the ones a new account starts with. An Echelon becoming Prospective keeps theirs.</li>
      <li><strong>Retired</strong> removes every team membership, then takes positions and roles
        back to those same defaults.</li>
      <li><strong>Inactive</strong> changes nothing else.</li>
      <li>Leaving <strong>Alpha</strong> removes the Alpha position, whichever status they move to.</li>
    </ul>
    Setting the status back afterwards does not return what was taken away.
  <% end %>
<% else %>
  <%= ui_callout_box :warning, icon: "triangle-exclamation", icon_type: :solid do %>
    <strong>A vintage callsign can never be released.</strong>
    The flag also makes the callsign show as a conflict in the handle checker, whatever the
    person's status. Only Council designates vintage callsigns.
    This page cannot take the flag back off — that is a per-person edit on their callsign.
  <% end %>
<% end %>
